    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GXSKz152TKYLU2Up3YFrPV)_\n\n## What\n\n- **Registry:** `sp-org-tag-registry.el` holds the note tags in `org-tag-persistent-alist`. The task tags stay in `org-tag-alist` (`sp-org-taskman-extra`).\n- **`M-x sp-org-tag-add`:** inserts a tag above a marker line in the registry file, saves it and runs `load-file`, so it works without restarting. It asks first if the tag is close to a registered one (typo guard).\n- **`M-x sp-org-tag-lint`:** scans the vault (vulpea db, else `~/notes`) and reports unregistered tags in `#+filetags:` and on headings, with the likely typo, plus notes with no `#+filetags:` (for `sp-tag-emoji`). `RET` visits, `a` registers, `g` reruns. `sp-org-tag-lint-buffer` does one file.\n- **`sp-org-create-note-and-link`** and **wikilink conversion:** both ask for at least one note tag (unknown ones can be registered on the spot) and write `#+filetags:`.\n- **`sp-split-leave-parents`:** binds `org-use-tag-inheritance` to the new `sp-split-inherit-tags` (nil), only while it runs.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The registry file is data, not tangled from a doc, because the command edits it. It is documented in `docs/tangles/funct/sp-org-tag-lint.org`.\n- Tangling `sp-vulpea.org` also moved two `defcustom`s in the split module from group `spcustom` to `sp-split`, which is what the doc already said.\n- #106 is stacked on this PR (it renames the split module).\n\n## Testing\n\n10 ERT tests (`tests/sp-org-tag-lint-test.el`) pass headless in Emacs 29.3, and `sp-org--write-note` was checked with tags. Not run against the real vault, vulpea or a GUI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BZJ5xQsEdMUBRHcJfgXvPb\n",
